<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ t("library.page.library-targum", "Library — targum") }}</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('tokens.css') }}{{ asset('shared.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('words.css') }}{{ asset('library.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
{#- The key, before anything that reads it (targum-internal#343). `building.js`, and
    the conversation's pill, the followed series and the palette in the nav, each read `window.TARGUM_KEY`
    once as they load; it was set in a script at the foot of the body, so on a local serve
    they held an empty key for the life of the page and the bell, the followed series and
    the chat list were refused. The hosted box has no key and was never affected. -#}
<script>window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";</script>
</head>
<body class="shelf">
{% set here = 'library' %}{% set title = t("nav.library", "Library") %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>

<main>
  {#- One list, not two. What the reader has built and what is waiting to be built are
      the same question — what shall I read — and splitting them into a shelf and a
      catalogue meant answering it twice, in two different shapes. The reader's own texts
      are on Your targums (design.md §12, "Yours and everyone's", 2026-09-25). -#}

  {#- See all's own head (board SeeAllDesk): the way back to the shelves, then the list's
      name in the serif with how many texts it holds — "All Hebrew texts 720", or the
      band it was opened from. The shell's "Library" stands down while it is up. -#}
  <p class="see-back" id="see-back" hidden><a href="/library" id="see-back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> {{ t("nav.library", "Library") }}</a></p>
  <h2 class="see-title" id="see-title" hidden></h2>

  {#- The search on the ground, the field the board draws (Library, SeeAllDesk), and on
      See all the three menus beside it: kind, level, language. Nothing else to choose
      before you start (design.md §12, "The Library stands on the ground"). The box is
      the one search, opened already held to the Library (design.md §12, "One search,
      everywhere", 2026-10-09): pressing it opens the search over the page. -#}
  <div class="lib-find" id="lib-find">
    <input
      id="find" class="well find" type="search" dir="auto" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
      placeholder="{{ t("library.page.search-box", "Search the Library") }}" aria-label="{{ t("library.page.search-box", "Search the Library") }}" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="palette">
    <div class="see-menus" id="see-menus" hidden></div>
  </div>

  {#- The kind doors (board Library: "Browse by kind"): the Tanakh's map, then News,
      Video, Books, the Weekly portion, the Mishnah and the rest of the Jewish texts — each
      a door to a place that already exists. Drawn by `library.js`. -#}
  <nav class="lib-doors" id="lib-doors" aria-label="{{ t("library.doors", "Browse by kind") }}" hidden></nav>

  {#- Where you are in the Jewish texts, once inside a door (targum-internal#340). -#}
  <nav class="crumbs" id="crumbs" aria-label="{{ t("library.page.where-you-are", "Where you are") }}" hidden></nav>
  <p class="note" id="picked-note" hidden></p>

  {#- The shelves, where the Library lands (design.md §12, "The Library is shelved by
      how much you'd follow", 2026-10-09): one row of texts for each band — Read it now,
      A stretch, Hard for now — and targum's own playlists, each a row of cards on the
      ground with a See all that is the list under that band. Drawn by `library.js`. -#}
  <div class="shelves" id="shelves" hidden></div>
  {#- The Weekly portion (targum-internal#411): this Shabbat's first, then the year onward
      from it. Among the Library's shelves, because "which portion is it this week" is
      asked every week and the list cannot answer it. Every card opens the portion's reader, which is
      built for everybody, so nothing here builds or spends (#410). Drawn by
      `library.js` from `/portions`, and only on the Hebrew shelf. -#}
  <section class="portions" id="portions" aria-labelledby="portions-head" hidden>
    <div class="portions-top">
      <h2 class="section-title portions-head" id="portions-head">{{ t("library.page.weekly-portion", "Weekly portion") }} <bdi class="portions-hebrew" lang="he" dir="rtl">פרשת השבוע</bdi></h2>
      <div class="seg" id="portion-schedule" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("library.page.which-calendar", "Which calendar") }}" hidden></div>
    </div>
    <ol class="portion-cards" id="portion-cards"></ol>
  </section>

  {#- The doors of the Jewish texts, as cards on the ground. -#}
  <ul class="cards" id="cards" hidden></ul>

  {#- See all, and a door's list: one card holding a table of rows (board SeeAllDesk) —
      the column heads, a row a text, and at its foot how many are showing, in what
      order, and Show more. Fifty at a time. -#}
  <section class="card see-list" id="picked" hidden>
    <div class="rows-head" id="rows-head" role="row"></div>
    <ul class="rows see-rows" id="catalogue"></ul>
    <p class="empty" id="picked-empty" hidden></p>
    <div class="see-foot" id="see-foot">
      <p class="tally" id="tally"></p>
      <button type="button" class="btn text see-more" id="see-more" hidden>{{ t("library.see.more", "Show more") }}</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Somebody who has just failed to find what they wanted is exactly who needs the
      add page. A link, not a form: this page's job is browsing. -#}
  <p class="elsewhere">{{ t("library.page.not-here", "Not here?") }} <a href="/add">{{ t("library.page.upload-your-own", "Upload your own") }}</a>.</p>
</main>
{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}

<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
window.TARGUM_CATALOGUE = {{ catalogue|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_COLLECTIONS = {{ collections|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_SETS = {{ sets|tojson }};
{% if strings %}window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};
{% endif %}</script>
<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('charts.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('scenes.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('subscribe.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('library.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
